{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Put every event a tracker tracks in a session, and sample whole sessions."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/sessions"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"Sessions","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"Sessions"}],"title":"Sessions","role":"collection"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sessions are opt-in. Add the sessions enricher to the ones a tracker is built with, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker’s worker sets each record’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionKey","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to its session’s identifier. A session goes on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"while each event comes less than the timeout (30 minutes by default) after the one before it,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measured between the records’ timestamps. The first event after a longer gap starts a new session.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The enricher tracks "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionStarted"},{"type":"text","text":" before each session’s first event, and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before that from the second session on, carrying the ended session’s duration. A run’s last session"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has no "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded"},{"type":"text","text":": a session ends only when an event comes after the timeout. Pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kinds:"},{"type":"text","text":" to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"track only one kind of session event, or neither; every record still carries its key."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A session’s identifier is a version 7 UUID: the session’s start in Unix milliseconds, then random","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bits. It is held in the enricher’s memory only, never written to disk, and a new tracker, as on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"next launch, starts a new session. Records a store kept from an earlier run carry no key.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sampler.sessions(rate:)"},{"text":" keeps or drops every record of a session alike, its session events with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it, by the record’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionKey"},{"text":". It needs the sessions enricher among the tracker’s enrichers.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For the app, device, operating system, locale and network an event was tracked on, use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StandardContext"},{"text":". For the app’s opens and moves to the background, use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LifecycleTracking"},{"text":":","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationOpened"},{"text":" after a long time in the background starts a new session here, though","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"neither module knows about the other.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Sessions